      "description": "Owner mobile navigation; route switching uses 768px on Diary and 640px elsewhere. Preview is in-flow; routing and permission filtering remain in MainLayout.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-nav\" aria-label=\"Primary navigation\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ds-nav-item\" aria-current=\"page\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M15 21v-8a1 1 0 0 0-1-1h-4a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v8\"></path><path d=\"M3 10a2 2 0 0 1 .709-1.528l7-6a2 2 0 0 1 2.582 0l7 6A2 2 0 0 1 21 10v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z\"></path></svg><span>Diary</span></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ds-nav-item\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M17.596 12.768a2 2 0 1 0 2.829-2.829l-1.768-1.767a2 2 0 0 0 2.828-2.829l-2.828-2.828a2 2 0 0 0-2.829 2.828l-1.767-1.768a2 2 0 1 0-2.829 2.829z\"></path><path d=\"m2.5 21.5 1.4-1.4\"></path><path d=\"m20.1 3.9 1.4-1.4\"></path><path d=\"M5.343 21.485a2 2 0 1 0 2.829-2.828l1.767 1.768a2 2 0 1 0 2.829-2.829l-6.364-6.364a2 2 0 1 0-2.829 2.829l1.768 1.767a2 2 0 0 0-2.828 2.829z\"></path><path d=\"m9.6 14.4 4.8-4.8\"></path></svg><span>Training</span></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ds-nav-item\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M22 12h-2.48a2 2 0 0 0-1.93 1.46l-2.35 8.36a.25.25 0 0 1-.48 0L9.24 2.18a.25.25 0 0 0-.48 0l-2.35 8.36A2 2 0 0 1 4.49 12H2\"></path></svg><span>Check-in</span></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ds-nav-item\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"1\"></circle><circle cx=\"19\" cy=\"12\" r=\"1\"></circle><circle cx=\"5\" cy=\"12\" r=\"1\"></circle></svg><span>More</span></button></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-nav{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));min-height:64px;border-top:1px solid hsl(var(--border));background:hsl(var(--background) / 0.9);backdrop-filter:blur(24px);padding:0 8px env(safe-area-inset-bottom);}.ds-nav-item{display:flex;flex:1;min-width:0;min-height:64px;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:4px;border:0;border-radius:0;padding:8px 4px;background:transparent;color:hsl(var(--muted-foreground));font:500 12px/16px var(--font-sans, 'Figtree Variable', sans-serif);transition:background-color 150ms cubic-bezier(0.4,0,0.2,1),color 150ms cubic-bezier(0.4,0,0.2,1);}.ds-nav-item svg{width:20px;height:20px;}.ds-nav-item[aria-current]{color:hsl(var(--primary));}.ds-nav-item:hover{background:hsl(var(--accent));color:hsl(var(--accent-foreground));}.ds-nav-item:focus-visible{outline:none;box-shadow:0 0 0 2px hsl(var(--background)),0 0 0 4px hsl(var(--ring));}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-nav-item{transition-duration:0.01ms;}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Badge",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "badge",
      "description": "Default informational status badge; no invented click behavior.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-badge\">Status</span>",
      "css": ".ds-badge{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:1px solid hsl(var(--primary) / 0.2);border-radius:calc(infinity * 1px);padding:4px 10px;background:hsl(var(--accent));color:hsl(var(--accent-foreground));font:500 12px/16px var(--font-sans, \"Figtree Variable\", sans-serif);transition:color 150ms cubic-bezier(0.4,0,0.2,1),background-color 150ms cubic-bezier(0.4,0,0.2,1);}.ds-badge:focus{outline:none;box-shadow:0 0 0 2px hsl(var(--background)),0 0 0 4px hsl(var(--ring));}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-badge{transition-duration:0.01ms;}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A calm instrument for one number at a time",
    "overview": "Night-navy surfaces, rounded numerals and quiet hairline rows make daily health data easy to scan on a phone. Dark is the hero treatment; light remains a complete theme. Periwinkle signals interaction while domain colors identify information. Foreground-filled actions are direct and restrained.\n\nThe finished redesign applies this language to Diary, Training Programs, the workout player and Check-in, with shared primitives carrying it into other routes. Metric panels, editable rows and charts share a family resemblance without forcing every screen into one composition. The existing SparkyFitness identity remains; the pinned visual direction changes the interface rather than the product name.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Rounded metric numerals with separate, quiet units.",
      "Hairline rows, flat cards and generous hero corners.",
      "Foreground-filled pill actions and periwinkle navigation states.",
      "Theme-aware domain markers, restrained charts and readable phone controls."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Action Fill Rule",
        "body": "Use `primary-fill` with `background` text for the default action. Reserve `primary` with `primary-foreground` for the explicit brand variant.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Token Format Rule",
        "body": "Wrap raw HSL triples in `hsl(var(--token))`; use the complete hex variables for macro and sleep-stage colors directly as `var(--token)`.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Numeral Rule",
        "body": "Use rounded type for measured values, counts and timers; keep headings, labels and units in Figtree.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Card Rule",
        "body": "Ordinary cards separate content with tone and hairlines. Floating overlays may use the existing soft shadows; the world is not shadow-free.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do use semantic colors and paired foregrounds in both themes.",
      "Do reuse Numeral, StatRows, MacroChips and TrendChart for the patterns they implement.",
      "Do let labels and values wrap, preserve visible focus, and retain coarse-pointer and safe-area rules.",
      "Do preserve real data, translated labels, permissions and existing interactions when styling a surface."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't substitute periwinkle for the foreground-filled default action.",
      "Don't treat domain marker colors as a guarantee of readable small text on every surface.",
      "Don't add decorative ring dashboards or multicolored card grids as the default summary language; use the implemented metric and row patterns.",
      "Don't inherit legacy uppercase eyebrows or tiny number-stepper buttons as new component standards."
    ]
  }
}
